set.body:
Extend the language-neutral wire IR additively from the durable constitution baseline.

Encode and validate:
- Op domain, codomain, role, evidence/certificate, representation, gauge, and provenance;
- secondOrder and compress derivations;
- FunctionalFrame and derived score/axis relationships;
- closed BaseObjective variants, normalization, parameter blocks, and result contracts;
- original versus lowered programs, proof-carrying rewrites, solver guarantee, residual certificates, and remaining result equivalence.

Acceptance:
- new nodes round-trip on JVM and JS;
- existing v0.1 valid and invalid conformance fixtures continue to behave identically;
- new invalid fixtures reject role/evidence conflation, illegal orientation, unsupported objective/normalization combinations, silent evidence upgrades, and broken rewrite provenance;
- payload identities remain stable for inline and external payloads;
- schema version changes are explicit and accompanied by migration/conformance fixtures.
